{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"for I know his inclination, which he is doing today\"</b> is like the reason for \"for now I know that you are a fearer of Elohim\" (Genesis 22:12) — this is knowledge in actuality, for knowledge of the future is knowledge in potentiality. And if Israel had not sinned in the wilderness and their inclination had not become known in actuality, it would not have been fitting to testify against them in a song, saying: \"It is revealed before Me that you will sin, and I testify against you that many evils and troubles such as this and that will befall you.\" Rather, what would have been appropriate would be to give them the Torah with general knowledge: \"If you are willing and hearken, you shall eat the good of the land; but if you refuse and rebel, you shall be devoured by the sword.\" But now that their evil inclination has become known to them as well, and their adulterous heart — it will tell them everything that will befall them, as it is said: \"Because I know that you are stubborn, and your neck is an iron sinew and your brow brass; and I told you from of old; before it came to pass I announced it to you\" (Isaiah 48:4–5)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:15:40.571305310Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}